        "original_id": "ad08437d-afc6-5552-b314-482ce6e1976c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Kluge, Sidney Salkow, Eva Maria Meineke\n- Works: Yesterday Girl, Something for Everyone\n- Topics: Film, New German Cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Salkow was born on June 16, 1911, and he was an American film director, screenwriter, and television director.\n- Alexander Kluge was born on 14 February 1932, and he is a German author, philosopher, academic, and film director.\n- Eva Maria Meineke appeared in more than one hundred films from 1942 to 2008.\n- Yesterday Girl, also titled Abschied von gestern and translated as Farewell to Yesterday, is a 1966 New German Cinema film written and directed by Alexander Kluge.\n- Eva Maria Meineke appeared in the films Yesterday Girl and Something for Everyone.\n- Sidney Salkow directed more than 50 motion pictures and died on October 18, 2000.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
